  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Brick Mosaic\n\nToy bricks drop in row by row from the bottom with a small bounce and build a pixel-art image on a baseplate. Give it a pixel-art grid as text in the pattern variable, or leave it empty for a built-in red disc.\n\nCategory: graphic-looks. Length: 2.84 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A logo, icon or emoji should be built out of toy bricks, one row at a time, for a playful reveal.\n- The image is simple enough to read as pixel art on a grid of about 10 to 40 cells across.\n- A kids, gaming or maker-themed video needs a build moment that feels hands-on.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The mark should assemble from a few geometric pieces that spin and snap into place: use puzzle-snap.\n- The build should rise as an isometric 3D city rather than a flat mosaic: use isometric-build.\n- The scene should melt into pixel streaks as a transition: use pixel-sort.\n\nVariables:\n- pattern (string): Pattern, default \"\"\n- colors (string): Colors, default \"{\\\"#\\\":\\\"#E5322D\\\",\\\".\\\":\\\"#FFFFFF\\\",\\\"x\\\":\\\"#111111\\\"}\"\n- cols (number, 6-40): Columns, default 24\n- rows (number, 4-24): Rows, default 14\n- row_delay (number, 1-8): Row delay, default 3\n- background (color): Baseplate, default \"#111111\"\n- speed (number, 0.1-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Brick Mosaic\n\n  Toy bricks drop in row by row from the bottom with a small bounce and build a pixel-art image on a baseplate. The image is a text grid in the pattern variable, one row per line (use / between rows), where each character is looked up in the colors variable; without a pattern it builds a red disc.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/brick-mosaic/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"brick-mosaic\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"2.84\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"pattern\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Pattern\", \"description\": \"Pixel art as text: rows separated by / , one character per cell. Characters are looked up in Colors; unknown characters and spaces leave the cell empty. Empty builds the default disc.\", \"default\": \"\"},\n    {\"id\": \"colors\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Colors\", \"description\": \"JSON map from pattern character to a CSS color.\", \"default\": \"{\\\"#\\\":\\\"#E5322D\\\",\\\".\\\":\\\"#FFFFFF\\\",\\\"x\\\":\\\"#111111\\\"}\"},\n    {\"id\": \"cols\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Columns\", \"description\": \"Grid columns of the default disc.\", \"default\": 24, \"min\": 6, \"max\": 40, \"step\": 1},\n    {\"id\": \"rows\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Rows\", \"description\": \"Grid rows of the default disc.\", \"default\": 14, \"min\": 4, \"max\": 24, \"step\": 1},\n    {\"id\": \"row_delay\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Row delay\", \"description\": \"Frames between rows.\", \"default\": 3, \"min\": 1, \"max\": 8, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"frames\"},\n    {\"id\": \"background\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Baseplate\", \"description\": \"Baseplate color behind the bricks.\", \"default\": \"#111111\"},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"Playback speed.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.1, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.1}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Brick Mosaic</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        #root { background: #111111; }\n        .bm-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; }\n        .bm-stage svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"brick-mosaic\" data-duration=\"2.84\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"bm-clip\" class=\"bm-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"2.84\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <svg id=\"bm-svg\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></svg>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              if (typeof value === \"boolean\") return value;\n              if (value === \"true\") return true;\n              if (value === \"false\") return false;\n              return fallback;\n            }\n            var FPS = 30;\n            var W = root.clientWidth || 1080;\n            var H = root.clientHeight || 1920;\n\n            // Seeded random in [0, 1): a string hash, so the same key always gives the same value.\n            function rnd(key) {\n              var h = 1779033703 ^ key.length;\n              for (var i = 0; i < key.length; i++) {\n                h = Math.imul(h ^ key.charCodeAt(i), 3432918353);\n                h = (h << 13) | (h >>> 19);\n              }\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 16), 2246822507);\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 13), 3266489909);\n              h ^= h >>> 16;\n              return (h >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n            }\n\n            // Piecewise-linear map of x from inR to outR, optionally eased per segment and clamped.\n            function interp(x, inR, outR, o) {\n              o = o || {};\n              var n = inR.length;\n              var i = 0;\n              if (x >= inR[n - 1]) i = n - 2;\n              else if (x > inR[0]) { while (x > inR[i + 1]) i++; }\n              var t = (x - inR[i]) / (inR[i + 1] - inR[i]);\n              if (o.clamp !== false) t = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, t));\n              if (o.easing) t = o.easing(t);\n              return outR[i] + (outR[i + 1] - outR[i]) * t;\n            }\n            function clamp01(t) { return Math.min(1, Math.max(0, t)); }\n\n            // Easings with the usual names; every one maps 0..1 to 0..1.\n            var E = {\n              linear: function (t) { return t; },\n              quad: function (t) { return t * t; },\n              cubic: function (t) { return t * t * t; },\n              sin: function (t) { return 1 - Math.cos((t * Math.PI) / 2); },\n              back: function (s) { return function (t) { return t * t * ((s + 1) * t - s); }; },\n              out: function (f) { return function (t) { return 1 - f(1 - t); }; },\n              inOut: function (f) { return function (t) { return t < 0.5 ? f(t * 2) / 2 : 1 - f((1 - t) * 2) / 2; }; },\n              bezier: function (x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n                return function (x) {\n                  if (x <= 0) return 0;\n                  if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                  var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                  for (var k = 0; k < 24; k++) {\n                    var mt = 1 - t;\n                    var bx = 3 * mt * mt * t * x1 + 3 * mt * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                    if (bx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                    t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                  }\n                  var m = 1 - t;\n                  return 3 * m * m * t * y1 + 3 * m * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n                };\n              }\n            };\n\n            var SVGNS = \"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\";\n            function el(tag, attrs, parent) {\n              var e = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, tag);\n              for (var k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]);\n              if (parent) parent.appendChild(e);\n              return e;\n            }\n\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            // Runs draw(frame) from the timeline so seeking to a time always draws the same picture.\n            function drive(frames, draw) {\n              var clock = { frame: 0 };\n              tl.to(clock, { frame: frames, duration: frames / FPS, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(clock.frame); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n            }\n\n            var cols = Math.round(num(vars.cols, 24, 6, 40)), rows = Math.round(num(vars.rows, 14, 4, 24));\n            var rowDelay = num(vars.row_delay, 3, 1, 8);\n            var speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.1, 4);\n            root.style.background = str(vars.background, \"#111111\");\n            var colors = { \"#\": \"#E5322D\", \".\": \"#FFFFFF\", x: \"#111111\" };\n            try {\n              var parsedColors = JSON.parse(str(vars.colors, \"\"));\n              if (parsedColors && typeof parsedColors === \"object\" && !Array.isArray(parsedColors)) colors = parsedColors;\n            } catch (e) { /* keep the default colors */ }\n\n            // The grid: text rows turned into a color per cell (\"\" leaves the cell empty).\n            var source;\n            var given = str(vars.pattern, \"\");\n            if (given) source = given.split(\"/\").map(function (row) { return row.replace(/\\s+$/, \"\"); });\n            else {\n              var ccx = (cols - 1) / 2, ccy = (rows - 1) / 2, rad = Math.min(cols, rows) * 0.4;\n              source = [];\n              for (var y = 0; y < rows; y++) { var line = \"\"; for (var x = 0; x < cols; x++) line += Math.hypot(x - ccx, y - ccy) <= rad ? \"#\" : \".\"; source.push(line); }\n            }\n            var grid = source.map(function (row) { return row.split(\"\").map(function (ch) { return Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(colors, ch) ? String(colors[ch]) : \"\"; }); });\n            var nRows = grid.length, nCols = Math.max.apply(null, [1].concat(grid.map(function (r) { return r.length; })));\n            var s = Math.min((W * 0.86) / nCols, (H * 0.86) / nRows);\n            var ox = (W - s * nCols) / 2, oy = (H - s * nRows) / 2;\n            var gap = s * 0.04, bevel = s * 0.09, stud = s * 0.28, b = s - gap;\n            var FALL = 7, HOP = 5;\n\n            var svg = document.getElementById(\"bm-svg\");\n            svg.setAttribute(\"viewBox\", \"0 0 \" + W + \" \" + H);\n            var defs = el(\"defs\", {}, svg);\n            var lg = el(\"linearGradient\", { id: \"bm-stud\", x1: 0.15, y1: 0.1, x2: 0.85, y2: 0.9 }, defs);\n            [[\"0\", \"#FFFFFF\", 0.5], [\"0.45\", \"#FFFFFF\", 0], [\"1\", \"#000000\", 0.22]].forEach(function (st) { el(\"stop\", { offset: st[0], \"stop-color\": st[1], \"stop-opacity\": st[2] }, lg); });\n            // Baseplate studs the bricks snap onto.\n            var plate = el(\"g\", { fill: \"#FFFFFF\", opacity: 0 }, svg);\n            grid.forEach(function (row, r) { row.forEach(function (_, c) { el(\"circle\", { cx: ox + (c + 0.5) * s, cy: oy + (r + 0.5) * s, r: stud }, plate); }); });\n            var bricks = [];\n            grid.forEach(function (row, r) {\n              row.forEach(function (color, c) {\n                if (!color) return;\n                var g = el(\"g\", { opacity: 0 }, svg);\n                el(\"rect\", { width: b, height: b, rx: s * 0.06, fill: color }, g);\n                el(\"path\", { d: \"M 0 \" + b + \" V 0 H \" + b + \" L \" + (b - bevel) + \" \" + bevel + \" H \" + bevel + \" V \" + (b - bevel) + \" Z\", fill: \"#FFFFFF\", opacity: 0.22 }, g);\n                el(\"path\", { d: \"M \" + b + \" 0 V \" + b + \" H 0 L \" + bevel + \" \" + (b - bevel) + \" H \" + (b - bevel) + \" V \" + bevel + \" Z\", fill: \"#000000\", opacity: 0.22 }, g);\n                el(\"circle\", { cx: b / 2 + s * 0.035, cy: b / 2 + s * 0.05, r: stud, fill: \"#000000\", opacity: 0.28 }, g);\n                el(\"circle\", { cx: b / 2, cy: b / 2, r: stud, fill: color }, g);\n                el(\"circle\", { cx: b / 2, cy: b / 2, r: stud, fill: \"url(#bm-stud)\" }, g);\n                bricks.push({ g: g, x0: ox + c * s + gap / 2, y0: oy + r * s + gap / 2, start: (nRows - 1 - r) * rowDelay + c * 0.12 + rnd(\"brick-\" + r + \"-\" + c) * 1.5 });\n              });\n            });\n            var outCubic = E.out(E.cubic);\n\n            function draw(frame) {\n              var t = frame * speed;\n              plate.setAttribute(\"opacity\", 0.07 * interp(t, [0, 10], [0, 1], { easing: outCubic }));\n              bricks.forEach(function (br) {\n                var local = t - br.start;\n                if (local < 0) { br.g.setAttribute(\"opacity\", 0); return; }\n                var y = 0;\n                if (local < FALL) { var p = local / FALL; y = -s * 1.8 * (1 - p * p); }\n                else if (local < FALL + HOP) { var q = (local - FALL) / HOP; y = -s * 0.12 * 4 * q * (1 - q); }\n                br.g.setAttribute(\"opacity\", interp(local, [0, 2], [0, 1]));\n                br.g.setAttribute(\"transform\", \"translate(\" + br.x0 + \" \" + (br.y0 + y) + \")\");\n              });\n            }\n            drive(Math.round(parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"2.84\") * FPS), draw);\n\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"2.84\");\n            if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"brick-mosaic\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
